    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="0363" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg283"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Iddings.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-07-20"><hi rendition="#italic">July 20,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hill directs that the Italian minister for foreign affairs be informed that
                    an investigation of the alleged lynching at Erwin of <pb facs="0364" n="284"
                        xml:id="pg284"/> persons born in Italy is being made by the governor of
                    Mississippi, and that all legal steps to secure justice which may be warranted
                    by the facts will be taken by this Government.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
